      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Hi, I’m Yamini.</h1>
      <p class="page-head__lead">I’m a podcast editor, producer, and educator who loves helping people tell their stories well.</p>
      <p>I see stories, I feel stories, and I love sharing them. As we swim in bite-sized content, data, and opinions, what truly connects us is a good story — and when you find one, you give it your time, your most precious resource.</p>
      <p>I created, host, and produce <em>Women of Wayland – The Podcast</em>, now in its fifth season. I’ve produced and edited podcasts for independent creators, reported as an episode correspondent for Peace Talks Radio, and taught podcasting through lectures, workshops, and small-group sessions.</p>
      <p>Learning, listening, and leading are the mantras I live by. I’m a performer and a problem solver at heart, and I bring both to every edit and every class.</p>
